WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.571
was the day of the winter science fair.

2
00:00:12.531 --> 00:00:15.652
Stella sat at a table with a jar of snow.

3
00:00:16.572 --> 00:00:20.693
There was a display with information about snowflakes behind her.

4
00:00:21.193 --> 00:00:23.514
Her friend's mom came over to the table.

5
00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.314
"Hey, Stella.

6
00:00:25.555 --> 00:00:26.875
What's your project about?"

7
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:28.795
Stella smiled.

8
00:00:28.815 --> 00:00:30.076
"Hi, Mrs.

9
00:00:30.136 --> 00:00:32.461
Singer. I did some research on snow."

10
00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:36.484
"That sounds interesting," Mrs.

11
00:00:36.564 --> 00:00:37.305
Singer said.

12
00:00:37.325 --> 00:00:41.208
"So, are you a snow expert now?"

13
00:00:42.048 --> 00:00:43.009
Stella grinned.

14
00:00:43.029 --> 00:00:44.750
"I'm not sure yet.

15
00:00:45.331 --> 00:00:47.252
But I learned how snow forms."

16
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:51.255
By now a couple of other adults stood nearby.

17
00:00:51.275 --> 00:00:54.277
"Let's hear about it," the man said.

18
00:00:54.297 --> 00:00:57.460
"Okay," Stella said.

19
00:00:58.292 --> 00:01:03.136
"First the outdoor temperature must be 0 degrees Celsius or below.

20
00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.338
That freezes the water vapor in the air.

21
00:01:07.318 --> 00:01:11.942
The frozen vapor then attaches to specks of dust and pollen.

22
00:01:12.602 --> 00:01:15.424
When this happens, tiny ice crystals form.

23
00:01:16.185 --> 00:01:20.187
Like all crystals, these have flat sides and sharp corners.

24
00:01:20.207 --> 00:01:26.412
"Some of the ice crystals stick together, forming clumps of crystals.

25
00:01:27.396 --> 00:01:29.078
They grow bigger and bigger.

26
00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:33.862
Eventually all these crystals fall to the ground as snow."

27
00:01:33.882 --> 00:01:37.145
"Hmm." Mrs.

28
00:01:37.225 --> 00:01:38.506
Singer rubbed her chin.

29
00:01:38.526 --> 00:01:44.352
"So, snowflakes are just clumps of ice crystals that are stuck together?"

30
00:01:45.212 --> 00:01:46.153
Stella nodded.

31
00:01:46.173 --> 00:01:50.517
"Some snowflakes have up to two hundred ice crystals."

32
00:01:50.537 --> 00:01:53.440
"Whoa!" the woman said.

33
00:01:53.996 --> 00:01:57.499
"Can you tell us what makes the ice crystals fall out of the clouds?"

34
00:01:57.519 --> 00:01:59.681
"Yes," Stella said.

35
00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:03.665
"But the ice crystals don't really fall out of the clouds.

36
00:02:04.385 --> 00:02:06.987
The ice crystals are the clouds.

37
00:02:07.608 --> 00:02:09.390
They are what clouds are made of.

38
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.252
"Oh," the woman said.

39
00:02:12.272 --> 00:02:16.075
"The bunches of ice crystals get heavy," Stella said.

40
00:02:16.095 --> 00:02:19.058
"That's when they fall to the ground as snow.

41
00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.080
It's the same thing with rain.

42
00:02:21.904 --> 00:02:24.266
Water vapor turns into water droplets.

43
00:02:25.007 --> 00:02:26.188
They join together.

44
00:02:26.889 --> 00:02:30.352
And when the droplets are heavy enough, they fall as rain."

45
00:02:32.093 --> 00:02:34.295
Mrs. Singer pointed to the poster.

46
00:02:34.315 --> 00:02:37.758
"Tell us about those pretty snowflakes."

47
00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:43.704
"Sure." Stella stood up so everyone could see the poster better.

48
00:02:43.724 --> 00:02:48.108
"My poster shows all the basic shapes of snowflakes.

49
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.041
Some are shaped like stars, needles, or plates.

50
00:02:52.921 --> 00:02:54.302
Others have little branches.

51
00:02:55.482 --> 00:02:58.643
Most snowflakes have six sides or six points.

52
00:02:59.443 --> 00:03:01.484
But every snowflake is different.

53
00:03:02.184 --> 00:03:05.965
In fact, you'll probably never find two that are exactly the same."

54
00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:09.086
"Huh," the man said.

55
00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:11.226
"Why are they all so different?"

56
00:03:11.246 --> 00:03:16.788
"Because ice crystals stick together in lots of different ways," Stella said.

57
00:03:17.788 --> 00:03:23.313
"Other things affect their shape too—like the air's temperature and its moisture levels.

58
00:03:25.395 --> 00:03:30.519
When there's just a little moisture in the air, snowflakes are shaped like flat plates.

59
00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.743
They're shaped like stars when there's more moisture in the air."

60
00:03:34.763 --> 00:03:37.585
"Very interesting!"

61
00:03:38.025 --> 00:03:38.786
the man said.

62
00:03:38.806 --> 00:03:40.507
"I never knew that."

63
00:03:40.527 --> 00:03:43.330
"Oh!" Stella said suddenly.

64
00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.632
"I just remembered one other thing.

65
00:03:46.464 --> 00:03:48.065
You know how snow looks white?

66
00:03:48.926 --> 00:03:53.109
Well, that's only because of how light reflects off all the crystals.

67
00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.711
Snow is actually clear."

68
00:03:55.731 --> 00:03:57.953
"Wow, Stella."

69
00:03:58.733 --> 00:04:00.514
Mrs. Singer smiled at her.

70
00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:03.497
"You are an expert on snow."

71
00:04:03.517 --> 00:04:05.278
"I guess I am."

72
00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:07.259
Stella smiled too.

73
00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:11.122
"To me, snowflakes are amazing!"
